# A slim closure that is given a property, frozen or moved below another object gets storage of its own at that moment, through the run time: 946 instructions for `f = () => a; f.tag = 1` where a full closure takes 153.
# So a function is given full closures where reached code does one of those to a value that holds its closures and no others. Reading `name` and `length`, calling, and looking for a name change nothing.
# It is an expectation: what unseen code does, or what is done through a value that may hold closures of several functions, is not in it, and costs time alone. Without a word of Link every one of these is slim.
# -- source: closures-changed.ts
